within AnomalyLibrary.UsersGuide;
class Conventions "Activation, interfaces and observable quantities"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Information;
  annotation(Documentation(info="<html><p>The usual internal activation interval is half open: <code>[startTime,endTime)</code>. An external trigger replaces that interval where <code>useExternalTrigger</code> is provided. Continuous effects may use a severity-scaled transition ramp; discrete effects require severity zero or one. Read each class for its supported settings.</p><p><code>active</code> describes the activation request or latch. It does not always mean that the effect has ended when it becomes false: transition ramps, captured commands and finite pulses can continue according to their own rules. Inspect <code>effectLevel</code>, <code>effectActive</code> or the component-specific physical quantities as applicable.</p><p>Use the declared connector orientation and SI units. For communication, a unit increase in <code>txCount</code> identifies a new frame, whereas <code>sequence</code> remains payload metadata. A held numerical output is not evidence of a newly delivered or valid frame; inspect <code>rxCount</code>, <code>available</code> and <code>validOut</code>.</p></html>"));
end Conventions;
